FGD gypsum is a synthetic byproduct generated during sulfur-dioxide removal at coal-fired power plants. Because it is chemically similar to natural gypsum, the material can be used in cement, drywall, soil conditioning and other construction applications. Demand is therefore linked to both environmental management at power facilities and downstream gypsum consumption.

